{title: 157 - Go to Dark Gethsemane}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #157 • GETHSEMANE • 6.8.7.7.7.7}
{lyricist: James Montgomery}
{composer: Richard Redhead}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 157}
{meta: tune GETHSEMANE}
{meta: meter 6.8.7.7.7.7}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Go to [Bb]dark [Eb]Gethsemane,
[Eb]Ye who [Cm]feel [Bb]the [Eb]tempter's [Bb]power
[Eb]Your [Cm]Redeemer's [Ab]conflict [Eb]see.
[Eb/G]Watch with [Bb/D]him [Gm]one [Eb]bitter [Bb]hour;
[Eb/G]Turn not [Fm]from [Eb]his [Ab]griefs away;
[Eb/G]Learn [Fm]from [Eb]Jesus Christ [Bb]to [Eb]pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]See Him [Bb]at [Eb]the [Ab]judgment [Eb]hall,
[Eb]Beaten, [Bb]bound, [Eb]reviled, [Bb]arraigned;
[Eb]See [Cm]Him [Bb]meekly [Ab]bearing [Eb]all;
[Eb/G]Love to [Bb/D]man [Gm]His [Eb]soul [Fm]sustained!
[Eb/G]Shun not suffering, [Ab]shame, or [Eb]loss;
[Eb/G]Learn [Fm]from [Eb]him [Fm/Ab]to [Eb/Bb]bear [Bb]the [Eb]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Calvary's [Bb]mournful [Ab]mountain [Eb]climb;
[Eb]There, [Cm]adoring [Ab]at [Bb]his [Eb]feet,
[Eb]Mark [Cm]that [Bb]miracle [Ab]of [Eb]time,
[Eb/G]God's own [Bb/D]sacrifice [Fm]complete.
[Eb/G]"It is [Fm]finished!" [Ab]hear him [Eb]cry;
[Eb/G]Learn [Fm]from [Eb]Jesus Christ [Bb]to [Eb]die.
{end_of_verse}
